course: dictionary
lesson: 15162
title: Scots: a word from Scotland
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scots is a word with three jobs. It can describe things from Scotland, like a Scots accent. It can name a language, the Scots language, which is close to English but has many of its own words. It can also name the people: the Scots are the people of Scotland. Look for the capital S, because it names a country's people or language.
explain: «My granny is Scots, and she was born in Glasgow.» Here Scots tells us where she is from: Scotland. «She says «wee» for small and «ken» for know.» Those words belong to the Scots language, so the context shows Scots is a language too. The words around it are your clues.
explain: «The Scots are proud of their castles and their hills.» Here Scots means the people. Ask yourself: is it describing a thing, naming a language, or naming people? Also, Scots is not the same as Gaelic. Gaelic is another language spoken in Scotland.
fact: Scots starts with a capital letter, because it names a country's people or language.
fact: Scotland is part of the UK, in the north of Great Britain.
fact: The Scots language has words like «wee» (small), «bairn» (child) and «ken» (know).
fact: Robert Burns wrote famous poems in Scots.
fact: Gaelic is a different language, also spoken in Scotland.
exercise: «My granny is Scots, and she was born in Glasgow.» What does Scots tell us here? | A kind of cake | A sport she likes to play | The colour of her hair | *Where she is from, Scotland
exercise: «She says «bairn» for child, which is a Scots word.» What is Scots a name for here? | A food | A sport | A type of bird | *A language
exercise: «Robert Burns wrote poems in Scots.» What is Scots in this sentence? | A lake | *A language | A football team | A mountain
test: «The Scots are friendly, and they welcomed us to Edinburgh.» Who are the Scots in this sentence? | *The people of Scotland | A Scottish dish | A kind of tree | A type of weather
test: Which word means small in Scots? | Gaelic | Ken | Bairn | *Wee
exam: Which sentence uses Scots to mean the people of Scotland? | He read a poem in Scots. | The Scots pine is a very tall tree. | Scots is a language spoken in Scotland. | *The Scots cheered for their team at the match.
